Download the file:
   WSLSetup.zip
Unzip the file
Open PowerShell as administrator
Run:
   Set-ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope CurrentUser
Open the file
Run:
   .\WSLInstall.ps1
Once it finishes, restart your computer
Wait for the WSL setup to launch, then when prompted, provide your desired username and password
Once set up, simply run "WSL" in your compand prompt or in your file explorer to launch your Ubuntu

For a quick setup, follow these instructions:
Move the WSLQuickSetup.sh file into your WSL user directory (The directory will show up at the bottom of your file explorer)
Run:
   sudo cmod +x WSLQuickSetup.sh
Run:
   sudo ./WSLQuickSetup.sh

For a full setup, follow these instructions:
Move the WSLFullSetup.sh file into your WSL user directory (The directory will show up at the bottom of your file explorer)
Run:
   sudo cmod +x WSLFullSetup.sh
Run:
   sudo ./WSLFullSetup.sh

To start your python virtual environment in order to be able to use pip install, use:
   source .venv/bin/activate
To close your virtual environment, Use:
   deactivate
